---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout
  title="FAQ · Cytidel"
  description="The questions security teams ask before choosing Cytidel — and how we answer them."
>
  <section class="hero faq-hero" aria-labelledby="hero-h1">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="hero-inner">
        <span class="eyebrow">FAQ</span>
        <h1 id="hero-h1">Frequently asked questions</h1>
        <p class="hero-sub">The questions security teams ask before choosing Cytidel — and how we answer them.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="faq" aria-labelledby="faq-h2">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 id="faq-h2" class="sr-only">Frequently asked questions</h2>
      <div class="faq-list" role="list">

        <details class="faq-item" role="listitem">
          <summary class="faq-q">
            <span>We already have Tenable / Qualys. Why do we need Cytidel?</span>
            <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          </summary>
          <div class="faq-a"><div class="faq-a-inner">
            Tenable and Qualys tell you what's vulnerable inside your environment. Cytidel tells you what's being exploited outside it — across thousands of sources including attacker forums, exploit repositories, social media, and threat actor campaigns. Your scanner shows you the backlog, once it has the signature. We tell you when a new zero-day drops, when exploit code appears in the wild, and when a vulnerability in your stack comes under active exploitation — often before your scanner can even see it. We work alongside the stack you already have, not instead of it.
          </div></div>
        </details>

        <details class="faq-item" role="listitem">
          <summary class="faq-q">
            <span>How does Cytidel's risk rating compare to Tenable VPR or Qualys TruRisk?</span>
            <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          </summary>
          <div class="faq-a"><div class="faq-a-inner">
            Tenable VPR and Qualys TruRisk prioritise within your scanned environment. Cytidel's risk rating tells you what attackers are doing with vulnerabilities right now — informed by exploitation evidence, proof-of-concept availability, threat actor activity, and live signals. Different purposes, and they work well together.
          </div></div>
        </details>

        <details class="faq-item" role="listitem">
          <summary class="faq-q">
            <span>What data do we need to share?</span>
            <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          </summary>
          <div class="faq-a"><div class="faq-a-inner">
            None. Cytidel does not require access to your internal environment. Our intelligence engine is built on external data sources. Integration with your scanner or ticketing system is available when you are ready — but it is not a prerequisite.
          </div></div>
        </details>

        <details class="faq-item" role="listitem">
          <summary class="faq-q">
            <span>How quickly can we get started?</span>
            <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          </summary>
          <div class="faq-a"><div class="faq-a-inner">
            Most teams are operational within 24 hours. Account creation takes minutes. We recommend starting with a demo so we can configure onboarding around your environment — the technology stack you care about and the suppliers you need to monitor.
          </div></div>
        </details>

        <details class="faq-item" role="listitem">
          <summary class="faq-q">
            <span>We do not have the resource for another tool.</span>
            <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          </summary>
          <div class="faq-a"><div class="faq-a-inner">
            Cytidel doesn't add to the manual intelligence workload — it replaces it. Teams report saving 20+ hours per analyst per week on manual research and report production. The capacity comes back to your team for incident response, threat hunting, and the work that needs a human.
          </div></div>
        </details>

        <details class="faq-item" role="listitem">
          <summary class="faq-q">
            <span>How is pricing structured?</span>
            <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          </summary>
          <div class="faq-a"><div class="faq-a-inner">
            Pricing is based on organisation size, not seat count. Every plan includes unlimited access for your security team. We will walk you through pricing on a call — bring your environment and the suppliers you need to monitor, and we'll show you what it looks like for you.
          </div></div>
        </details>

        <details class="faq-item" role="listitem">
          <summary class="faq-q">
            <span>How do you track threat actors?</span>
            <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          </summary>
          <div class="faq-a"><div class="faq-a-inner">
            Cytidel's threat actor intelligence maps every known adversary to the CVEs in their arsenal, with full TTP context, alias tracking, and campaign history. When a threat actor starts targeting software you depend on, you know — with the evidence and the context to act. The full module is called Villain Vault, and the best way to see it work is in a demo.
          </div></div>
        </details>

        <details class="faq-item" role="listitem">
          <summary class="faq-q">
            <span>Are you ISO 27001 certified?</span>
            <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          </summary>
          <div class="faq-a"><div class="faq-a-inner">
            Yes. Cytidel is ISO 27001:2022 certified. We've also designed the platform to support customers going through their own ISO 27001 assessments — automating intelligence gathering and mapping scans against current threat activity.
          </div></div>
        </details>

        <details class="faq-item" role="listitem">
          <summary class="faq-q">
            <span>We are an MSSP. Can we use Cytidel's intelligence?</span>
            <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          </summary>
          <div class="faq-a"><div class="faq-a-inner">
            Yes. Our OEM programme is live and already integrated with a partner product in market. We also have an MSSP programme available. Reach out to our partnerships team directly — these are strategic conversations that deserve a dedicated discussion.
          </div></div>
        </details>

      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="final-cta" aria-labelledby="final-cta-h2">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 id="final-cta-h2">Have a question we haven't answered?</h2>
      <p>Book a 20-minute call. Bring your specific question — pricing, integrations, threat actor coverage, ISO 27001, MSSP programme — and we'll walk you through it.</p>
      <a href="/book-a-demo" class="btn btn-primary">
        Book a Demo
        <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<script>
  // Single-open FAQ accordion. <details> handles toggle natively; we add
  // close-others behaviour after the native toggle has fired.
  const items = document.querySelectorAll<HTMLDetailsElement>('.faq-item');
  items.forEach((item) => {
    const summary = item.querySelector('.faq-q');
    summary?.addEventListener('click', () => {
      setTimeout(() => {
        if (item.open) {
          items.forEach((other) => {
            if (other !== item) other.removeAttribute('open');
          });
        }
      }, 0);
    });
  });
</script>

<style>
  /* Container + section defaults — match the original page */
  .container {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 1280px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding-left: clamp(20px, 4vw, 48px);
    padding-right: clamp(20px, 4vw, 48px);
  }
  section {
    padding-top: clamp(48px, 6vw, 88px);
    padding-bottom: clamp(48px, 6vw, 88px);
  }

  /* Hero — base + .faq-hero override */
  .hero {
    padding-top: clamp(80px, 11vw, 140px);
    padding-bottom: clamp(56px, 8vw, 100px);
    position: relative;
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .hero::before {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    top: -200px;
    left: 50%;
    transform: translateX(-50%);
    width: 1200px;
    height: 700px;
    background: radial-gradient(ellipse at center, rgba(128, 252, 19, 0.18) 0%, transparent 65%);
    pointer-events: none;
    z-index: 0;
  }
  .hero-inner { position: relative; z-index: 1; }
  .faq-hero {
    padding-top: clamp(80px, 10vw, 120px);
    padding-bottom: clamp(40px, 5vw, 60px);
  }
  .faq-hero .hero-sub { margin-top: 20px; }

  .eyebrow {
    display: inline-block;
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--color-accent-deep);
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
  }

  .hero h1 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: -0.028em;
    line-height: 1.06;
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--color-text);
    font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 5.6vw, 4rem);
  }
  .hero-sub {
    margin: 28px 0 0;
    font-size: clamp(1.05rem, 1.55vw, 1.22rem);
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
  }

  /* Visually-hidden helper for the off-screen FAQ h2 */
  .sr-only {
    position: absolute;
    width: 1px; height: 1px;
    padding: 0; margin: -1px;
    overflow: hidden;
    clip: rect(0, 0, 0, 0);
    white-space: nowrap;
    border: 0;
  }

  /* FAQ list */
  .faq-item {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }
  .faq-q {
    width: 100%;
    background: transparent;
    border: none;
    color: var(--color-text);
    padding: 22px 0;
    text-align: left;
    font-size: clamp(1rem, 1.5vw, 1.12rem);
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: -0.005em;
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 24px;
    transition: color 0.15s ease;
    cursor: pointer;
    list-style: none; /* hide native <summary> marker */
  }
  .faq-q::-webkit-details-marker { display: none; }
  .faq-q:hover { color: var(--color-accent-deep); }
  .faq-q:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid var(--color-accent);
    outline-offset: 4px;
    border-radius: 4px;
  }
  .faq-q .icon {
    flex-shrink: 0;
    width: 20px;
    height: 20px;
    position: relative;
    color: var(--color-text-tertiary);
  }
  .faq-q .icon::before,
  .faq-q .icon::after {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    background: currentColor;
    top: 50%;
    left: 50%;
    transform-origin: center;
    transition: transform 0.2s ease;
  }
  .faq-q .icon::before { width: 14px; height: 1.5px; transform: translate(-50%, -50%); }
  .faq-q .icon::after  { width: 1.5px; height: 14px; transform: translate(-50%, -50%); }
  .faq-item[open] .faq-q { color: var(--color-text); }
  .faq-item[open] .faq-q .icon::after { transform: translate(-50%, -50%) scaleY(0); }

  .faq-a {
    max-height: 0;
    overflow: hidden;
    transition: max-height 0.3s ease;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
  }
  .faq-item[open] .faq-a { max-height: 1600px; }
  .faq-a-inner {
    padding: 0 0 28px;
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  /* Final CTA (FAQ-specific copy + Book a Demo button) */
  .final-cta {
    text-align: center;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }
  .final-cta h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: -0.018em;
    line-height: 1.08;
    color: var(--color-text);
    font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 3vw, 2.4rem);
    margin: 0 0 20px;
  }
  .final-cta p {
    font-size: clamp(1.02rem, 1.5vw, 1.15rem);
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    margin: 0 0 36px;
    max-width: 640px;
    margin-left: auto;
    margin-right: auto;
  }

  /* Buttons */
  .btn {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    padding: 14px 22px;
    border-radius: 10px;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 0.98rem;
    transition: transform 0.15s ease, background 0.15s ease, box-shadow 0.2s ease;
    border: 1px solid transparent;
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  .btn-primary {
    background: #80FC13;
    color: #0b2000;
  }
  .btn-primary:hover {
    transform: translateY(-1px);
    box-shadow: 0 8px 30px rgba(128, 252, 19, 0.35);
  }
  .btn .arrow { transition: transform 0.2s ease; }
  .btn:hover .arrow { transform: translateX(3px); }
</style>
